 "defenses": [
  {
   "against": "BNS 303",
   "argument": "The prosecution has failed to prove the essential ingredient of 'dishonest intention' (animus furandi). The facts merely state that the accused moved the motorcycle without permission; they do not establish a specific intent to permanently deprive the owner of possession. Mere unauthorized movement, especially when the vehicle was left in a public lane and the accused rode it away immediately, does not automatically satisfy the legal requirement of dishonesty absent evidence of concealment, denial of ownership, or refusal to return the property.",
   "fact_quote": "The accused had no permission to take it and did not return it.",
